A||||16||Ed||Paint My Wagon||||5||
Z||000000||Ed||01-18-2000||11:24 PM||||OK folks, I'm open to suggestions. I've been thinking about getting my '87 black GT painted. I'm not going to do it: Do any of you have suggestions about where to have it done? Chains v. small shops? Going through a GM dealer to their sub? Our local club president had Maaco do his Formula and it came out very well in metallic green. Unfortunately, that particular shop is too far away for me to use. <P>The second part of the question is: What color? The car is now black with a saddle (brown to the less retentive types on the board) interior.  Coverage of lighter colors over black? I'm kinda inclined to the oranges and yellows. And price? And do shops have to be reminded about the flexible, plastic body?<P>Let 'er rip.<p>[This message has been edited by Ed (edited 01-19-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||01-18-2000||11:58 PM||||I personally prefer to have a local shop do all my painting. But then again, I am part owner of that shop and I must say they do really good work. (Shameless Plug!) Basic paint job on one of our cars is in the $700 range. Located in north east Alabama, might even make arrangements to meet half way to pick up a car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||01-19-2000||01:21 AM||||OK. Good price. I'll meet you in New Mexico!<P>So, what color shall we paint it? ||||reg||4
Z||000003||Cooter||01-19-2000||08:36 PM||||Cool! $700 to paint the car, $700 to pick up and deliver. Let me get a substitute for the next few days and I will be on my way.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||01-19-2000||11:15 PM||||The only good body shop that I really trust around here wants twice that much for a paint job on my 85 GT. They do body work to a lot of hotrods and customs around here. Other than the clear coat failing and some rock chips in the nose, the body is in good condition. I figured a guy could get a good job done cheaper, somewhere. Let's see, a road trip to sweet home Alabama in order to save $700. I could stop over to Ed Park's and pick up an engine and other parts for my dead 87 SE too. There is that Fiero swap meet thing sort of down that way later this spring.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||01-20-2000||12:40 AM||||Y'all come to Cooterville and we will have a painting party! I have had at least 5 VW bugs in the shop at one time in different stages of restoration, so 5 Fieros should fit and still have working room. Sounds like fun to me, as long as Monkeyman will behave himself!||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||01-20-2000||09:15 AM||||If I had vacation time, and money, you could sign me up.||||reg||1
Z||000007||deceler8||01-20-2000||02:42 PM||||Just out of curiousity, if five people (or twenty...whatever) decided to meet at a central point and all agreed on the same color, what would it cost to paint a car in that situation...<P>And assuming everyone had body work, sanding, etc. done beforehand...<P>I've got it...Fiero Paint-A-Thon 2000...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||01-20-2000||03:05 PM||||Good question! If 5 people had their cars and helped each other tape up and do the final prep, basically the only charges would be for materials and paint booth usage. That would be a cool way to get stuff done. Like an old time quilting party! Wouldn't grandmaw be proud!||||reg||1
Z||000009||william_thorniii||01-20-2000||03:09 PM||||Cooter,<P>Since we are all talking Fiero's here, wouldn't it be easier to remove our panels and shoot them off of the car?  I have always wondered about that.  Also do you paint on weekends?  If so, what is your turn around time?  <P>Many Thanks,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000010||batboy||01-20-2000||05:19 PM||||I'll bring the beer for the Cooterville painting party. Monkey will be ok as long as he has his meds...LOL. Hmmm, beer and meds don't really mix well, hmmm, maybe that will be fun too. Just joking!||||reg||1
Z||000011||william_thorniii||01-20-2000||05:56 PM||||Batboy,<P>As long as Monkey isn't the one with the paint gun, I think that we will all be alright... well not alright, but safe anyway.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000012||Cooter||01-20-2000||08:53 PM||||I pull some panels off the car to make painting them easier: The rear spoiler, lower rockers, etc. If I were changing the color on the car, I'd probably take off more of the panels, but you run the risk of scratching the fresh paint trying to get everything bolted back together. Having the car all apart is nice for the guy painting, but harder for the guy putting it all back together. But I still try to take all practical bolt on parts off to make sure the area around them gets good surface prep.<BR>Because painting cars is part time, I cant really say about a turn around time. Some days I have faculty meetings and dont get any time at the body shop while others I may get 3 or 4 hours in after school. When school gets out for long weekends or summer is when I can really get some stuff done.<p>[This message has been edited by Cooter (edited 01-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||william_thorniii||01-20-2000||09:05 PM||||Cooter,<P>O.K. then if I were to head down in the summer, could we paint the car on a weekend.  I prefer to disassemble as much as possible and take the chance of scratching it.  If you think that this is possible, I might consider it this summer.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000014||Cooter||01-20-2000||09:27 PM||||My main concern is the drying time of the paint. I like for one to sit inside for at least 24 hours before moving it out into the weather. I still believe that it would be possible to do in a weekend, but it might take a couple of late nighters.||||reg||1
Z||000015||batboy||01-20-2000||11:24 PM||||Maybe we ought to start a Cooterville Paint Party topic and give Ed back his topic.<P>Sorry Ed for taking over this thread. Hey, I'm a poet and didn't even know it.<P>In case anyone forgot, he's asking for suggestions on color of paint. I can't believe the "any color as long as it's red" crowd hasn't spoken up yet. Ed mentioned he likes orange, now that's a color I haven't seen on a Fiero yet, very original. Maybe a nice Competition Orange like some of the 69 Z-28s I've seen in the past.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cooter||01-20-2000||11:46 PM||||Okay 86Se, get the Photoshop running and paint us an orange Fiero! My 88GT is painted the wrong color, it looks orange next to my 85, but a true orange might look good, or well, like an orange. ||||reg||1
